statement:
Let $Y,Z$ be integral schemes [def-weil-pbc-scheme-conventions, def-sbc-normal-dominant-galois] and $g:Y	o Z$ a dominant morphism. Suppose every local ring of $Y$ is integrally closed. For the absolute normalization $
u:Z^{
u}	o Z$ [def-sc-normalization], there is a unique dominant morphism $f:Y	o Z^{
u}$ with $
u\circ f=g$. No quasi-compactness, Noetherian, or finite-type hypothesis is imposed.
